G2228.b:
⟪ἤ⟫, disjunctive and comparative particle (Bl., §36, 12; 77, 11);
⟪1.⟫ disjunctive, ⟪or⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ between single words: ⟦Matthew 5:17|Mt 5:17⟧, ⟦Mark 6:56|Mk 6:56⟧, ⟦Luke 2:24|Lk 2:24⟧, ⟦John 6:19|Jo 6:19⟧, ⟦Romans 1:21|Ro 1:21⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ before a sentence expressing a variation, denial or refutation of a previous statement, freq. in interrog. form: ⟦Matthew 7:4|Mt 7:4⟧, ⟦Matthew 7:9|9⟧, ⟦Mark 12:14|Mk 12:14⟧, ⟦Luke 13:4|Lk 13:4⟧, ⟦Romans 3:29|Ro 3:29⟧ ⟦Romans 6:3|6:3⟧ ⟦Romans 9:21|9:21⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:9|I Co 6:9⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:16|16⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 9:6|9:6⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:7|II Co 11:7⟧; ἢ . . . ἤ, ⟪either . . . or⟫, ⟦Matthew 6:24|Mt 6:24⟧, ⟦Luke 16:13|Lk 16:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:6|I Co 14:6⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ in a disjunctive question (as Lat. an after utrum): ⟦Matthew 9:5|Mt 9:5⟧, ⟦Mark 2:9|Mk 2:9⟧, ⟦Luke 7:19|Lk 7:19⟧, al.; after πότερον, ⟦John 7:17|Jo 7:17⟧; μή, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:8|I Co 9:8⟧; μήτι, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:17|II Co 1:17⟧; ἢ . . . ἢ . . . ἤ, ⟦Mark 13:35|Mk 13:35⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Comparative, ⟪than⟫: after comparatives, ⟦Matthew 10:15|Mt 10:15⟧, ⟦Luke 9:13|Lk 9:13⟧, ⟦John 3:19|Jo 3:19⟧, ⟦Romans 13:11|Ro 13:11⟧, al.; after ἕτερον, ⟦Acts 17:21|Ac 17:21⟧; θέλω (Khüner3, ɪᴠ, 303), ⟦1 Corinthians 14:19|I Co 14:19⟧; πρὶν ἤ, ⟪before⟫, seq. acc. et inf., ⟦Matthew 1:18|Mt 1:18⟧, ⟦Mark 14:30|Mk 14:30⟧; after a positive adj. (⟦Genesis 49:12|Ge 49:12⟧; cf. Robertson, Gr., 661), ⟦Matthew 18:8|Mt 18:8⟧, ⟦Matthew 18:9|9⟧, ⟦Mark 9:43|Mk 9:43⟧, ⟦Mark 9:45|45⟧, ⟦Mark 9:47|47⟧.
⟪3.⟫ With other particles: ἀλλ’ ἤ, v.s. ἀλλά; ἢ γάρ, v.s. γάρ; ἢ καί, ⟪or even⟫, ⟪or also⟫, ⟦Matthew 7:10|Mt 7:10⟧, ⟦Luke 11:11|Lk 11:11⟧, ⟦Luke 11:12|12⟧, ⟦Romans 2:15|Ro 2:15⟧ ⟦Romans 4:9|4:9⟧, al.; ἤτοι . . . ἤ, ⟦Romans 6:16|Ro 6:16⟧ (cf. Wi 11:19).

G2244.b:
⟪ἡλικία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< ἧλιξ, of the same age, mature), [in LXX: ⟦Ezekiel 13:18|Ez 13:18⟧ (⁨קוֹמָה⁩), ⟦Job 29:18|Jb 29:18⟧, Wi 4:9, Si 26:17, freq. in II-IV Mac;] always of age or maturity; "a stage of growth whether measured by age or stature";
⟪1.⟫
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪age⟫: ⟦Matthew 6:27|Mt 6:27⟧, ⟦Luke 12:25|Lk 12:25⟧ (R, mg.), ⟦Hebrews 11:11|He 11:11⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪full age⟫, ⟪maturity⟫: ⟦John 9:21|Jo 9:21⟧, ⟦John 9:23|23⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:13|Eph 4:13⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪stature⟫: ⟦Luke 19:3|Lk 19:3⟧ (⟦Matthew 6:27|Mt 6:27⟧, ⟦Luke 12:25|Lk 12:25⟧, AV, R, txt.; but the prevailing usage in LXX and π. favours the former meaning in these doubtful passages; cf., Ellic., ICC, AR, on ⟦Ephesians 4:13|Eph 4:13⟧; Milligan, NTD, 74 f., and esp., MM, Exp., xv; e contra, Field, Notes, 6).†

G2270.b:
⟪ἡσυχάζω⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨שׁקט⁩;] ⟪to be still⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to rest from labour⟫: ⟦Luke 23:56|Lk 23:56⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to live quietly⟫: ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:11|I Th 4:11⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to be silent⟫: ⟦Luke 14:3|Lk 14:3⟧, ⟦Acts 11:18|Ac 11:18⟧ ⟦Acts 21:14|21:14⟧ (cf. ⟦Job 32:7|Jb 32:7⟧, ⟦Nehemiah 5:8|Ne 5:8⟧).†
SYN.: σιγάω (q.v.), σιωπάω.
